menu "NFC Card Storage"

    config KERN_NFC
        bool "Enable NFC card storage (M5Stack RFID Unit 2 or PN532)"
        default y
        help
            Compile support for keeping KEF-encrypted mnemonics on NFC cards,
            read and written through an external reader on the board's I2C
            bus: an M5Stack RFID Unit 2 (WS1850S) or a PN532 module. Whichever
            is plugged in is found at runtime.

            Building it in does not turn it on: the feature stays inert until
            it is also enabled at runtime under Settings -> NFC, which is off
            by default. The RF field is energized only while the card page is
            open.

    config KERN_NFC_WS1850S
        bool "Support the M5Stack RFID Unit 2 (WS1850S)"
        default y
        depends on KERN_NFC

    config KERN_NFC_I2C_ADDR
        hex "WS1850S I2C address"
        default 0x28
        depends on KERN_NFC_WS1850S
        help
            7-bit I2C address of the reader. 0x28 is the M5Stack RFID Unit 2
            factory default.

    config KERN_NFC_PN532
        bool "Support PN532 modules (Elechouse V3 and clones)"
        default y
        depends on KERN_NFC
        help
            The red "PN532 NFC RFID V3" board and its clones. Set the module's
            mode switch to I2C and power it from 3.3 V: its pull-ups tie SDA
            and SCL to its own supply, and the bus is shared with the touch
            controller.

    config KERN_NFC_PN532_I2C_ADDR
        hex "PN532 I2C address"
        default 0x24
        depends on KERN_NFC_PN532
        help
            7-bit I2C address of the PN532. Fixed at 0x24 by the chip.

    config KERN_NFC_I2C_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "I2C transaction timeout (ms)"
        default 100
        depends on KERN_NFC
        help
            Per-transfer timeout for reader access. Bounds every blocking call
            so an absent or wedged module cannot stall the UI.

endmenu
